[center][size=6][b][color=#f0bd77]Romestead Content Forge[/color][/b][/size]
[i]Add your own items, weapons, creatures, dungeons and more to Romestead with JSON content packs — ready-made AI and behaviors included, C# optional. No game files edited.[/i][/center]

[quote][b]Version 1.0.1 — works with the Romestead 2026-10-04 update. Provided as-is — fixes when I have time, no promises.[/b]
I made this for myself and may fix things now and then, but I can't promise updates or a timeline. It's experimental: much of it is tested, some features aren't, and future game updates can break things. The full source is on [url=https://github.com/kvotheous/RomesteadContentForge]GitHub[/url] (MIT license) — anyone is welcome to fork it, fix it or build on it.[/quote]

[line]

Content Forge is a modding framework: drop a [i].json[/i] "content pack" in a folder and it injects brand-new content straight into the game's databases at load. Your creations behave like real game content — they spawn, equip, deal damage, heal, craft, and show up in the [b]Item Spawner[/b] automatically.

[size=5][b][color=#f0bd77]Easiest way to start: the Forge Editor[/color][/b][/size]
Don't want to write JSON by hand? Download [b]ForgeEditor-<version>.zip[/b], unzip, and run [b]ForgeEditor.exe[/b] (no Python, no install):
[list]
[*][b]Every game value is built in[/b] — items, creatures, icons, sounds, effects and more are picked from dropdowns, so you never guess an id.
[*][b]Forms for every field[/b], with PNG previews and per-language text.
[*][b]Built-in dialogue editor[/b] — write NPC conversations (Yarn) with syntax highlighting, a node outline, error checks, and a side-by-side translation grid that tracks how much is translated.
[*][b]One-click validation[/b] catches mistakes before you launch the game.
[*]It saves the same [i].json[/i] packs the mod reads, so you can switch between the editor and hand-editing anytime.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#f0bd77]More than an injector: built-in building blocks[/color][/b][/size]
It's not just a content injector: Content Forge ships ready-made systems your packs can use by name.
[list]
[*][b]Creature AI[/b]: [b]8 ready-made AI brains[/b]: guard, coward, ranged caster, patroller, pack hunter, summoner, healer, turret. Give any creature one by name.
[*][b]Interactive objects[/b]: [b]ready-made behaviors[/b] for placeables: crafting stations, portals, healing shrines, levers, talking objects (dialogue), props and multi-part buildings, plus a data-driven animation controller for fully custom creatures.
[*][b]World events[/b]: [b]wave defense, boss rush, hunt contest, scheduled raids, team battles, king of the hill, races[/b] and PvP duel arenas, all configured in JSON.
[*][b]Dialogue commands[/b]: NPC conversations can [b]give items, take payment and heal[/b] ([i]ForgeGiveItem[/i], [i]ForgeTakeItem[/i], [i]ForgeHeal[/i]).
[*][b]C# when you want it[/b]: addon DLLs can register their [b]own behaviors and AI[/b] with one call, and any pack can then use them by name (see [url=https://github.com/kvotheous/RomesteadContentForge/blob/main/docs/ADVANCED.md]Advanced[/url]).
[*][b]Worked examples[/b]: [b]3 example packs[/b] (a story world, a necromancer class, and a test pack covering every feature) plus a [b]cookbook[/b] of copy-paste recipes.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#f0bd77]What you can make[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Items[/b] — anything: name, description, icon, tier, stack size, sell/buy price.
[*][b]Icons[/b] — reuse any in-game icon, [b]or import your own .png[/b].
[*][b]Gear[/b] — helmets/armor/boots/trinkets/capes with [b]stat bonuses[/b] (health, crit, move speed, damage, resistances…).
[*][b]Weapons (full stats)[/b] — [b]melee[/b] (swords, spears, daggers, sledgehammers, fists) and [b]ranged[/b] (bows, crossbows, javelins): damage by element, knockback, reach, [b]stagger/stun[/b], [b]move-speed-while-swinging[/b], [b]charged heavy attacks[/b], [b]proc chance[/b] (e.g. 25% ignite), on-hit auras, and [b]+stat bonuses while held[/b].
[*][b]Shields[/b] — custom block strength and arc.
[*][b]Spells, scrolls, wands & staves[/b] — projectile/status spells cast by an Offhand [b]spell-tome[/b] or a melee weapon that fires [b]on swing[/b] (a staff with a real animation) or [b]on hit[/b] (ignite/poison weapons).
[*][b]Composed spells[/b] — a spell can [b]chain[/b] others on impact: an arrow that spawns lightning, a fireball that also ignites. Chains nest for multi-stage effects.
[*][b]Custom held looks[/b] — reuse a vanilla model, [b]recolor[/b] one with a custom [b]palette[/b] (dye), or paint your [b]own held sprite sheet[/b].
[*][b]Swing trails[/b] — recolor the slash, replace its [b]shape[/b] with your own art, or [b]hide[/b] it (for staves).
[*][b]Custom VFX[/b] — your own sprite-animation effects, or reskin a vanilla effect.
[*][b]Custom sounds[/b] — reuse the game's audio, or just ship your own [b]wav/ogg/mp3/flac[/b] files (FMOD banks also supported for advanced setups).
[*][b]Loot[/b] — add your items to [b]mob/chest drop tables[/b] with a % chance — or straight onto a [b]creature[/b] (wildlife included: bears and wolves can finally drop your items).
[*][b]Summons (necromancer)[/b] — a spell can spawn creatures that [b]fight for you[/b] (skeletons, skulls, wolves…), with a per-cast [b]count[/b] and a [b]max-active cap[/b] (oldest despawns). Set each to [b]guardian[/b] (stays put) or [b]companion[/b] (blinks to your side when you wander off).
[*][b]Playable classes[/b] — add a [b]profession to character creation[/b] (skill head-start + starting gear/clothes/favour). The bundled [b]Necromancer[/b] example ships a class, a 2-skeleton book, a staff, a robe and a recipe.
[*][b]World quests[/b] — auto-activating [b]kill/collect/loot/craft/harvest[/b] quests that [b]unlock crafting recipes[/b] when finished — no NPC or dialogue needed.
[*][b]Placeable furniture[/b] — buildable [b]decorations in the construction menu[/b], reusing vanilla art with your own name, icon, build cost and footprint. The recipe auto-unlocks so it's always available.
[*][b]Custom creatures[/b] — clone a vanilla creature into an [b]elite/recolored variant[/b] (new id, [b]more health[/b], [b]color tint[/b], custom name) reusing its AI, then summon it like any creature.
[*][b]Brand-new monsters from your art[/b] — [b]from-scratch sprite animations[/b] (no vanilla art at all) plus [b]8 built-in AI brains[/b] (guard, coward, ranged caster, patroller, pack hunter, summoner, healer, turret): a fully custom creature from one PNG.
[*][b]Custom dungeons & worlds[/b] — author maps in the [b]free Tiled editor[/b]: [b]multi-room dungeons[/b] (doors link rooms) with an [b]overworld entrance[/b] new worlds roll like any vanilla one — or [b]retrofit into your EXISTING save[/b] — plus per-map [b]music, ambience and ambient light[/b]. No game tools needed.
[*][b]Portals[/b] — a placeable that [b]teleports players into your custom world[/b] from anywhere (and back).
[*][b]Dialogue NPCs[/b] — talking characters in your maps, written as plain-text [b]YarnSpinner[/b] files (lines, options, conditions, portraits) with per-language translations. Dialogue can [b]check your bag, take payment, give items and heal[/b] — merchants, quest-givers, lore drops.
[*][b]Interactive placeables[/b] — healing [b]shrines[/b], [b]levers[/b], [b]talking statues/gravestones[/b], props and portals: server-authoritative, save-persistent, optional [b]indestructible[/b] flag for quest temples.
[*][b]Custom art everywhere[/b] — placeables can ship [b]their own sprite[/b] (with ambient animation), and custom creatures accept [b]fully repainted animation rigs[/b].
[*][b]Player skins[/b] — new [b]hair styles in character creation[/b], reskins of vanilla character parts, and brand-new [b]worn armor looks[/b] your items can wear (dyeable via palettes).
[*][b]Custom skills[/b] — real [b]skills-screen entries[/b] (icon, localized name, levels 0–100, favour on level-up) trained by your weapons and spells.
[*][b]Favour-tree nodes[/b] — new nodes in the gods' favour tree (stat bonuses / auras / recipe unlocks), [b]uninstall-safe[/b] (removing a pack auto-refunds the point — never blocks login).
[*][b]Forge tab[/b] — a "Forge" toggle in the Skills & Favours window lists installed packs, pack skills and learned pack favours.
[*][b]Custom favour screen[/b] — packs can ship their [b]own fullscreen favour tree[/b] (vanilla look: draggable grid, connection lines, click to unlock) behind a "Pack Favours" button in the Skills & Favours window.
[*][b]Announcement banners[/b] — event/arena/mod messages as [b]big red text top-center[/b] (or the classic toast) — style, color, position, duration configurable in RomesteadContentForge.cfg.
[*][b]Drop-in sounds[/b] — put a .wav/.ogg next to your pack and use it for spell casts, shrines, portals. No audio tools needed.
[*][b]Swing-arc control[/b] — melee weapons can sweep any cone width (a 300° whirl-cleaver is one line of JSON).
[*][b]Player body rigs[/b] — tint or repaint the player's animated body itself, every frame.
[*][b]More spell behaviors[/b] — multi-shot fans, [b]lingering AoE pools[/b], [b]explosions[/b], self/party [b]heals[/b] — and [b]casting requirements[/b] (skill level, favour, quest, class) with a custom denial message.
[*][b]PvP zones & duel arenas[/b] — flag a map [b]pvp: true[/b] and players can fight inside it (no item loss on death there; player damage stays blocked everywhere else). Bind an [b]arena[/b] to it: kill announcements in chat, timed matches, an item prize for the winner.
[*][b]Co-op mod handshake[/b] — joining clients report their installed packs; the host gets chat warnings about missing packs, version mismatches, or unmodded players.
[*][b]World events[/b] — wave-defense arenas, boss rushes, timed hunt contests, scheduled vanilla raids — plus [b]team battles[/b], [b]king-of-the-hill[/b] and [b]checkpoint races[/b] — all from JSON.
[*][b]Custom citizens[/b] — new town workers with fixed names, looks and job mastery; edit vanilla citizen types too.
[*][b]Town workshops & work recipes[/b] — clone a vanilla job-building into your own buildable workshop and teach its workers [b]new recipes[/b] (a Grand Bakery that bakes [i]your[/i] bread).
[*][b]Multi-part buildings[/b] — compose several sprites, each with its own collision box, into [b]ONE buildable monument[/b] with walkable gaps.
[*][b]Deep weapon feel[/b] — per-combo-step damage/arc/timing, [b]two-handed weapons[/b], custom effect animations, retimed player animations — and a tool that turns [b]one drawing into a full held-weapon sheet[/b].
[*][b]Custom crafting stations[/b] — your placeable opens its own crafting window with its own recipes.
[*][b]Pre-placed map props[/b] — campfires, chests, any entity or your own PNG (with collision) directly in your maps.
[*][b]Visual asset catalog[/b] — one command generates a browsable HTML of every game sprite + all referenceable ids.
[*][b]Quest item rewards[/b] and [b]vanilla-dungeon interior replacement[/b].
[*][b]Crops & farming[/b] — plantable seeds with growth stages; farmsteads auto-farm them.
[*][b]Shops[/b] — new stock sections at the Market.
[*][b]Custom particles & emitters[/b] — your own particle textures and emitter shapes for torches, shrines, auras.
[*][b]Multi-language[/b] — names/descriptions per language; follows the player's game language. NPC dialogue translates too.
[*][b]Consumables[/b] (food/potions), [b]light sources[/b] (torches), and [b]crafting recipes[/b].
[/list]
Many packs coexist safely: each declares an [b]id / namespace / version / dependencies[/b], so different authors' content never collides. A [b]visual editor[/b] ([i]ForgeEditor.exe[/i]) is available for those who'd rather not write JSON.

[size=5][b][color=#f0bd77]How it works[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install the mod. On first run it creates a packs folder with a [b]working sample pack[/b] and a demo custom icon.
[*]Edit or add [i].json[/i] files there (and drop [i].png[/i] icons alongside).
[*]Launch — your content is in the game. Spawn it via [b]Item Spawner (F1)[/b], craft it, or find it where you placed it.
[/list]
Full authoring guide with every field, valid values, stat keys, and damage types is in [b]docs/PACKS.md[/b] in the Authoring zip (also on [url=https://github.com/kvotheous/RomesteadContentForge/blob/main/docs/PACKS.md]GitHub[/url]).

A taste:
[code]{
  "id": "mymod",
  "strings": { "mymod:flameblade:name": "Flameblade" },
  "items": [
    { "id": "mymod:flameblade", "name": "mymod:flameblade:name", "icon": "sword:iron", "tier": 5,
      "equippable": { "equipmentType": "Weapon", "displayId": "cdd:iron_sword",
        "weapon": { "class": "Sword", "minDamage": { "pyro": 80 }, "maxDamage": { "pyro": 120 } } } }
  ]
}[/code]

