[size=5][b][color=#f0bd77]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Romestead[/b]
[*][b]Romestead BepInEx Mod Loader[/b] (BepInEx 6 for .NET/CoreCLR) — required dependency. Install it first.
[*][b]Romestead Item Spawner[/b] (recommended) — to easily spawn and test your created items.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#f0bd77]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Which file do I download?[/b]
[list]
[*][b]RomesteadContentForge-<version>.zip[/b] — the mod itself ([i]BepInEx\plugins\[/i] DLLs). [b]Everyone needs this[/b].
[*][b]RomesteadContentForge-Authoring-<version>.zip[/b] — the [b]creator kit[/b]: all docs (field reference, cookbook, getting-started), the editor's Python source (for the ready-to-run app, get [i]ForgeEditor-<version>.zip[/i]), art/asset tools, worked example packs and 17 id catalogs. Only for pack [b]creators[/b]; unzips anywhere (nothing installs into the game).
[*][b]ForgeEditor-<version>.zip[/b] — optional standalone GUI editor ([i]ForgeEditor.exe[/i], no Python needed), for creators who want just the editor.
[/list]
Each download includes [i]THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt[/i] — the licenses of the open-source libraries it bundles.

[list=1]
[*]Install the [b]Romestead BepInEx Mod Loader[/b] and confirm it works.
[*]Download this mod's archive and extract it [b]into your Romestead game folder[/b] (the archive has the correct [i]BepInEx\plugins\[/i] layout).
[*]Launch once — the sample pack appears in [i]BepInEx\config\RomesteadContentForge\packs\[/i].
[*]Edit the sample or add your own packs, then relaunch.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#f0bd77]Notes & Compatibility[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Game updates:[/b] built for the Romestead [b]2026-10-04[/b] update. If a later update breaks part of the mod, that feature switches itself off (the BepInEx log shows "Patch ... failed") and the rest keeps working.
[*][b]Co-op:[/b] the [b]host[/b] must run the mod (content is server-authoritative); ideally all players run it with the [b]same packs[/b]. Against an unmodded host, modded content won't be present.
[*][b]Dedicated servers:[/b] not supported. Content Forge works in single-player and in co-op where a player hosts from the game.
[*][b]Save-safe:[/b] if you remove a pack, its items turn into harmless placeholders in old saves — no crashes.
[*][b]Custom icons[/b] should be authored at [b]18×18[/b] (the game's item-icon size) with a transparent margin.
[*]Pairs with the author's other Romestead mods (Item/Building/Citizen/Creature Spawners, Map Travel, Cheat Menu, QoL).
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#f0bd77]Source code & contributing[/color][/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/kvotheous/RomesteadContentForge]github.com/kvotheous/RomesteadContentForge[/url] — MIT licensed. Fork it, fix it, or send a pull request. There's also an unfinished [b]Werewolf Village[/b] game mode (social deduction: wolves, villagers, a seer, its own village map and art) on the [i]werewolf[/i] branch, if anyone wants to pick it up.

